learning/S083/evidence/raw/source/backlog.working.snapshot:413: trailing whitespace.
+### W001 conductor flow
learning/S083/evidence/raw/source/backlog.working.snapshot:414: trailing whitespace.
+
learning/S083/evidence/raw/source/backlog.working.snapshot:415: trailing whitespace.
+1. Select a host and inspect ring membership and current frontend/API/worker versions.
learning/S083/evidence/raw/source/backlog.working.snapshot:416: trailing whitespace.
+2. Prepare the candidate and run internal validation without claiming that production users have migrated.
learning/S083/evidence/raw/source/backlog.working.snapshot:417: trailing whitespace.
+3. Promote the pilot ring; observe its actual client journeys for the configured window.
learning/S083/evidence/raw/source/backlog.working.snapshot:418: trailing whitespace.
+4. Expand through subsequent rings only when readiness, compatibility, capacity, correctness, and latency gates pass.
learning/S083/evidence/raw/source/backlog.working.snapshot:419: trailing whitespace.
+5. Inject a bounded candidate regression; show halted later-ring promotion and the recovery behavior.
learning/S083/evidence/raw/source/backlog.working.snapshot:420: trailing whitespace.
+6. Restore, complete promotion, and export per-ring and aggregate transition evidence.
learning/S083/evidence/raw/source/backlog.working.snapshot:421: trailing whitespace.
+
learning/S083/evidence/raw/source/backlog.working.snapshot:422: trailing whitespace.
+Track ring rollout state separately from deployment state: a version can be ACTIVE for one ring while another ring remains pending. Logical cohorts do not automatically isolate shared compute, databases, or queues.
learning/S083/evidence/raw/source/backlog.working.snapshot:423: trailing whitespace.
+
learning/S083/evidence/raw/source/backlog.working.snapshot:424: trailing whitespace.
+### W002 conductor flow
learning/S083/evidence/raw/source/backlog.working.snapshot:425: trailing whitespace.
+
learning/S083/evidence/raw/source/backlog.working.snapshot:426: trailing whitespace.
+1. Provision getProfile v1 and v2 as separate revisions on ACA or version-specific Deployments/Services on AKS, within the same leased orchestrator environment.
learning/S083/evidence/raw/source/backlog.working.snapshot:427: trailing whitespace.
+2. Open a normal-user client and an authorized-preview client:
learning/S083/evidence/raw/source/backlog.working.snapshot:428: trailing whitespace.
+
learning/S083/evidence/raw/source/backlog.working.snapshot:429: trailing whitespace.
+   ```text
learning/S083/evidence/raw/source/backlog.working.snapshot:430: trailing whitespace.
+   Stable getProfile endpoint
learning/S083/evidence/raw/source/backlog.working.snapshot:431: trailing whitespace.
+       Default audience           -> v1, GA
learning/S083/evidence/raw/source/backlog.working.snapshot:432: trailing whitespace.
+       Authorized preview audience -> v2, private preview
learning/S083/evidence/raw/source/backlog.working.snapshot:433: trailing whitespace.
+   ```
learning/S083/evidence/raw/source/backlog.working.snapshot:434: trailing whitespace.
+
learning/S083/evidence/raw/source/backlog.working.snapshot:435: trailing whitespace.
+3. Confirm that direct and indirect v2 access rejects unauthorized preview callers. A feature flag, obscure URL, or 0% traffic weight is not the security boundary.
learning/S083/evidence/raw/source/backlog.working.snapshot:436: trailing whitespace.
+4. Observe both live versions, shared resource/dependency pressure, user state, and API contract behavior. Preview/GA eligibility is metadata separate from readiness and deployment lifecycle.
learning/S083/evidence/raw/source/backlog.working.snapshot:437: trailing whitespace.
+5. Approve v2 for broader production exposure and promote controlled cohorts or rings.
learning/S083/evidence/raw/source/backlog.working.snapshot:438: trailing whitespace.
+6. Make v2 the default across all browser, mobile, API, and microservice entry points; handle pinned users and older clients through the approved compatibility policy.
learning/S083/evidence/raw/source/backlog.working.snapshot:439: trailing whitespace.
+7. Verify actual migration and zero unintended new v1 admission; finish or safely transfer existing v1 work.
learning/S083/evidence/raw/source/backlog.working.snapshot:440: trailing whitespace.
+8. Exercise the retained compatible rollback path without discarding v2 writes; keep any interruptions in the result.
learning/S083/evidence/raw/source/backlog.working.snapshot:441: trailing whitespace.
+9. Complete promotion again, satisfy retention/drain/ownership gates, retire v1, and export the evidence.
learning/S083/evidence/raw/source/backlog.working.snapshot:442: trailing whitespace.
+
learning/S083/evidence/raw/source/backlog.working.snapshot:443: trailing whitespace.
+If v1/v2 denote breaking API contracts rather than deployment versions, the walkthrough must use an adapter or explicit client migration. Backend routing alone cannot force old consumers onto an incompatible contract and satisfy zero interruption.
learning/S083/evidence/raw/source/backlog.working.snapshot:444: trailing whitespace.
+
learning/S083/evidence/raw/source/backlog.working.snapshot:445: trailing whitespace.
