learning/S083/evidence/raw/source/readme.working.snapshot:148: trailing whitespace.
+### Scenario 1: Warm, overlapping blue-green handoff
learning/S083/evidence/raw/source/readme.working.snapshot:149: trailing whitespace.
+
learning/S083/evidence/raw/source/readme.working.snapshot:150: trailing whitespace.
+```gherkin
learning/S083/evidence/raw/source/readme.working.snapshot:151: trailing whitespace.
+Scenario: Move users to a warmed candidate without abandoning existing work
learning/S083/evidence/raw/source/readme.working.snapshot:152: trailing whitespace.
+    Given an Azure Web App has a live production deployment
learning/S083/evidence/raw/source/readme.working.snapshot:153: trailing whitespace.
+        And the current and candidate deployments are independently routable
learning/S083/evidence/raw/source/readme.working.snapshot:154: trailing whitespace.
+        And sufficient compute and dependency capacity exists for their overlap
learning/S083/evidence/raw/source/readme.working.snapshot:155: trailing whitespace.
+    When a candidate slot or parallel deployment is provisioned
learning/S083/evidence/raw/source/readme.working.snapshot:156: trailing whitespace.
+        And its endpoint and deployment identity are registered as WARMING
learning/S083/evidence/raw/source/readme.working.snapshot:157: trailing whitespace.
+        And required instances, dependencies, configuration, and journeys pass readiness gates
learning/S083/evidence/raw/source/readme.working.snapshot:158: trailing whitespace.
+        And its state is changed to READY
learning/S083/evidence/raw/source/readme.working.snapshot:159: trailing whitespace.
+        And eligible new admissions are routed to the candidate
learning/S083/evidence/raw/source/readme.working.snapshot:160: trailing whitespace.
+    Then migrated journeys preserve authentication, state, correctness, and latency budgets
learning/S083/evidence/raw/source/readme.working.snapshot:161: trailing whitespace.
+        And already-admitted work finishes or continues through a tested durable handoff
learning/S083/evidence/raw/source/readme.working.snapshot:162: trailing whitespace.
+        And actual routing and drain progress are verified
learning/S083/evidence/raw/source/readme.working.snapshot:163: trailing whitespace.
+        And the old deployment remains available for remaining clients and required rollback
learning/S083/evidence/raw/source/readme.working.snapshot:164: trailing whitespace.
+        And retirement occurs only after routing, drain, ownership, and retention gates pass
learning/S083/evidence/raw/source/readme.working.snapshot:165: trailing whitespace.
+```
learning/S083/evidence/raw/source/readme.working.snapshot:166: trailing whitespace.
+
learning/S083/evidence/raw/source/readme.working.snapshot:167: trailing whitespace.
+This scenario uses controlled routing rather than assuming a native slot swap permits application-controlled draining. S002 covers native swaps separately. Creating another slot in the same plan still requires adequate shared capacity.
learning/S083/evidence/raw/source/readme.working.snapshot:168: trailing whitespace.
+
learning/S083/evidence/raw/source/readme.working.snapshot:169: trailing whitespace.
+### Scenario 2: Progressive cohort or A/B routing
learning/S083/evidence/raw/source/readme.working.snapshot:170: trailing whitespace.
+
learning/S083/evidence/raw/source/readme.working.snapshot:171: trailing whitespace.
+```gherkin
learning/S083/evidence/raw/source/readme.working.snapshot:172: trailing whitespace.
+Scenario: Introduce a warmed candidate through stable traffic cohorts
learning/S083/evidence/raw/source/readme.working.snapshot:173: trailing whitespace.
+    Given production and candidate deployments are ready and compatible
learning/S083/evidence/raw/source/readme.working.snapshot:174: trailing whitespace.
+        And session, authentication, and persistent state remain valid across both
learning/S083/evidence/raw/source/readme.working.snapshot:175: trailing whitespace.
+        And sufficient capacity exists for the expected traffic distribution
learning/S083/evidence/raw/source/readme.working.snapshot:176: trailing whitespace.
+    When a small stable cohort is routed to the candidate
learning/S083/evidence/raw/source/readme.working.snapshot:177: trailing whitespace.
+        And actual candidate journeys are measured
learning/S083/evidence/raw/source/readme.working.snapshot:178: trailing whitespace.
+        And allocation is increased only after the acceptance gates pass
learning/S083/evidence/raw/source/readme.working.snapshot:179: trailing whitespace.
+    Then users remain uninterrupted during the routing transition
learning/S083/evidence/raw/source/readme.working.snapshot:180: trailing whitespace.
+        And a 50/50 A/B distribution can operate while both deployments remain healthy
learning/S083/evidence/raw/source/readme.working.snapshot:181: trailing whitespace.
+        And regressions stop further exposure and trigger the tested recovery path
learning/S083/evidence/raw/source/readme.working.snapshot:182: trailing whitespace.
+        And interruptions already experienced remain recorded as failures
learning/S083/evidence/raw/source/readme.working.snapshot:183: trailing whitespace.
+        And old-destination retirement waits for verified migration and drain completion
learning/S083/evidence/raw/source/readme.working.snapshot:184: trailing whitespace.
+```
