learning/S083/evidence/raw/source/readme.working.snapshot:194: trailing whitespace.
+### A. Deployment and traffic-migration strategies
learning/S083/evidence/raw/source/readme.working.snapshot:195: trailing whitespace.
+
learning/S083/evidence/raw/source/readme.working.snapshot:196: trailing whitespace.
+| ID | Scenario and required behavior |
learning/S083/evidence/raw/source/readme.working.snapshot:197: trailing whitespace.
+| --- | --- |
learning/S083/evidence/raw/source/readme.working.snapshot:198: trailing whitespace.
+| S001 | **Warm blue-green handoff:** Prepare green while blue serves users; migrate traffic only after readiness and compatibility validation. |
learning/S083/evidence/raw/source/readme.working.snapshot:199: trailing whitespace.
+| S002 | **Prepared native slot swap:** Validate staging with target configuration, address unsupported in-flight work, and make production the swap target. |
learning/S083/evidence/raw/source/readme.working.snapshot:200: trailing whitespace.
+| S003 | **Progressive canary:** Move through small traffic increments with journey-based acceptance gates before each increase. |
learning/S083/evidence/raw/source/readme.working.snapshot:201: trailing whitespace.
+| S004 | **50/50 A/B operation:** Keep cohorts stable and ensure both versions preserve equivalent state and transaction semantics. |
learning/S083/evidence/raw/source/readme.working.snapshot:202: trailing whitespace.
+| S005 | **Tenant-by-tenant migration:** Move one tenant at a time without splitting ownership of its state or background work. |
learning/S083/evidence/raw/source/readme.working.snapshot:203: trailing whitespace.
+| S006 | **Opt-in preview:** Allow authorized selected users into the candidate without breaking login, callbacks, or normal production navigation. |
learning/S083/evidence/raw/source/readme.working.snapshot:204: trailing whitespace.
+| S007 | **Session-boundary migration:** Send new sessions to green while active journeys finish on blue. |
learning/S083/evidence/raw/source/readme.working.snapshot:205: trailing whitespace.
+| S008 | **Release-ring migration:** Route users through matching frontend, API, and worker versions when mixed versions are incompatible. |
learning/S083/evidence/raw/source/readme.working.snapshot:206: trailing whitespace.
+| S009 | **Shadow traffic:** Replay safe traffic against green without duplicate writes, notifications, or external side effects. |
learning/S083/evidence/raw/source/readme.working.snapshot:207: trailing whitespace.
+| S010 | **Feature-flag activation:** Deploy compatible code first, then enable behavior progressively without another disruptive deployment. |
learning/S083/evidence/raw/source/readme.working.snapshot:208: trailing whitespace.
+
learning/S083/evidence/raw/source/readme.working.snapshot:209: trailing whitespace.
+### B. Actual capacity-scaling strategies
learning/S083/evidence/raw/source/readme.working.snapshot:210: trailing whitespace.
+
learning/S083/evidence/raw/source/readme.working.snapshot:211: trailing whitespace.
+| ID | Scenario and required behavior |
learning/S083/evidence/raw/source/readme.working.snapshot:212: trailing whitespace.
+| --- | --- |
learning/S083/evidence/raw/source/readme.working.snapshot:213: trailing whitespace.
+| S011 | **Manual horizontal scale-out:** Add instances and verify effective capacity before increasing their traffic share. |
learning/S083/evidence/raw/source/readme.working.snapshot:214: trailing whitespace.
+| S012 | **CPU/memory-driven scale-out:** Scale before resource saturation causes queuing or latency-budget violations. |
learning/S083/evidence/raw/source/readme.working.snapshot:215: trailing whitespace.
+| S013 | **Concurrency/queue-driven scale-out:** Use supported workload metrics to increase capacity before excessive request accumulation. |
learning/S083/evidence/raw/source/readme.working.snapshot:216: trailing whitespace.
+| S014 | **Scheduled or predictive scaling:** Provision and warm capacity before a known demand spike. |
learning/S083/evidence/raw/source/readme.working.snapshot:217: trailing whitespace.
+| S015 | **Horizontal scale-in:** Use host-supported admission, drain, or continuation mechanisms to preserve work before capacity terminates. |
learning/S083/evidence/raw/source/readme.working.snapshot:218: trailing whitespace.
+| S016 | **Autoscale oscillation:** Apply suitable stabilization so repeated scale-out/scale-in does not repeatedly interrupt users. |
learning/S083/evidence/raw/source/readme.working.snapshot:219: trailing whitespace.
+| S017 | **Vertical scaling through replacement:** Prepare a larger parallel deployment when an in-place size change would violate continuity requirements. |
learning/S083/evidence/raw/source/readme.working.snapshot:220: trailing whitespace.
+| S018 | **Independent tier scaling:** Scale the constrained tier while preserving contracts and capacity limits in remaining tiers. |
learning/S083/evidence/raw/source/readme.working.snapshot:221: trailing whitespace.
+| S019 | **Cell-based expansion:** Add an isolated application cell and migrate selected tenants through controlled state and routing handoff. |
learning/S083/evidence/raw/source/readme.working.snapshot:222: trailing whitespace.
+| S020 | **Quota or maximum-capacity exhaustion:** Preserve existing service using reserved capacity, block unsafe transitions, and report unsupported demand explicitly. |
learning/S083/evidence/raw/source/readme.working.snapshot:223: trailing whitespace.
+
learning/S083/evidence/raw/source/readme.working.snapshot:224: trailing whitespace.
+### C. Readiness and warm-up
learning/S083/evidence/raw/source/readme.working.snapshot:225: trailing whitespace.
+
learning/S083/evidence/raw/source/readme.working.snapshot:226: trailing whitespace.
+| ID | Scenario and required behavior |
learning/S083/evidence/raw/source/readme.working.snapshot:227: trailing whitespace.
+| --- | --- |
learning/S083/evidence/raw/source/readme.working.snapshot:228: trailing whitespace.
+| S021 | **Per-instance readiness:** Verify every required candidate instance, not whichever instance answers one endpoint probe. |
learning/S083/evidence/raw/source/readme.working.snapshot:229: trailing whitespace.
+| S022 | **Dependency-aware readiness:** Validate required database, cache, messaging, and service connectivity before admitting users. |
learning/S083/evidence/raw/source/readme.working.snapshot:230: trailing whitespace.
+| S023 | **Representative journey warm-up:** Exercise safe login, read, and transaction paths using isolated test fixtures. |
learning/S083/evidence/raw/source/readme.working.snapshot:231: trailing whitespace.
+| S024 | **Production-configuration validation:** Confirm effective production settings work without accidentally executing production background work. |
learning/S083/evidence/raw/source/readme.working.snapshot:232: trailing whitespace.
+| S025 | **Runtime and cache warm-up:** Prime JVM/JIT, application initialization, connection pools, and critical caches before exposure. |
learning/S083/evidence/raw/source/readme.working.snapshot:233: trailing whitespace.
+| S026 | **Slow image pull or startup:** Keep production serving while the candidate downloads its image and initializes. |
learning/S083/evidence/raw/source/readme.working.snapshot:234: trailing whitespace.
+| S027 | **False-positive health response:** Reject candidates whose probe returns an error, redirect, or misleading success response. |
learning/S083/evidence/raw/source/readme.working.snapshot:235: trailing whitespace.
+| S028 | **Warm-up timeout:** Abort explicitly and leave existing production routing intact. |
learning/S083/evidence/raw/source/readme.working.snapshot:236: trailing whitespace.
+| S029 | **Flapping readiness:** Require a suitable stable readiness window rather than promoting after one successful response. |
learning/S083/evidence/raw/source/readme.working.snapshot:237: trailing whitespace.
+| S030 | **Warm-up overload:** Limit initialization concurrency so candidate preparation does not overwhelm shared dependencies. |
learning/S083/evidence/raw/source/readme.working.snapshot:238: trailing whitespace.
+
learning/S083/evidence/raw/source/readme.working.snapshot:239: trailing whitespace.
+### D. Sessions, authentication, and user state
learning/S083/evidence/raw/source/readme.working.snapshot:240: trailing whitespace.
+
learning/S083/evidence/raw/source/readme.working.snapshot:241: trailing whitespace.
+| ID | Scenario and required behavior |
learning/S083/evidence/raw/source/readme.working.snapshot:242: trailing whitespace.
+| --- | --- |
learning/S083/evidence/raw/source/readme.working.snapshot:243: trailing whitespace.
+| S031 | **Externalized sessions:** Preserve session state when successive requests reach different instances or deployments. |
learning/S083/evidence/raw/source/readme.working.snapshot:244: trailing whitespace.
+| S032 | **Slot-routing cookie transition:** Observe and safely migrate pinned users before retiring their destination. |
learning/S083/evidence/raw/source/readme.working.snapshot:245: trailing whitespace.
+| S033 | **Worker-affinity removal:** Disable instance affinity only after eliminating or safely migrating instance-local state. |
learning/S083/evidence/raw/source/readme.working.snapshot:246: trailing whitespace.
+| S034 | **Authentication-key continuity:** Keep cookie/token validation compatible across deployments and planned key rotation. |
learning/S083/evidence/raw/source/readme.working.snapshot:247: trailing whitespace.
+| S035 | **Login callback during cutover:** Complete an OAuth/OIDC flow started before migration without redirect loops or forced reauthentication. |
learning/S083/evidence/raw/source/readme.working.snapshot:248: trailing whitespace.
+| S036 | **Existing form submission:** Accept valid anti-forgery tokens generated before migration without weakening validation. |
learning/S083/evidence/raw/source/readme.working.snapshot:249: trailing whitespace.
+| S037 | **Session serialization change:** Read existing session payloads during mixed-version operation. |
learning/S083/evidence/raw/source/readme.working.snapshot:250: trailing whitespace.
+| S038 | **Tenant authorization continuity:** Preserve permissions and isolation after routing changes. |
learning/S083/evidence/raw/source/readme.working.snapshot:251: trailing whitespace.
+| S039 | **Instance-local temporary state:** Move required uploads, workflow state, or generated artifacts to suitable shared/durable storage. |
learning/S083/evidence/raw/source/readme.working.snapshot:252: trailing whitespace.
+| S040 | **Cookie-less clients:** Preserve mobile and API-client continuity without assuming browser slot-routing cookies exist. |
learning/S083/evidence/raw/source/readme.working.snapshot:253: trailing whitespace.
+
learning/S083/evidence/raw/source/readme.working.snapshot:254: trailing whitespace.
+### E. In-flight requests and long-lived work
learning/S083/evidence/raw/source/readme.working.snapshot:255: trailing whitespace.
+
learning/S083/evidence/raw/source/readme.working.snapshot:256: trailing whitespace.
+| ID | Scenario and required behavior |
learning/S083/evidence/raw/source/readme.working.snapshot:257: trailing whitespace.
+| --- | --- |
learning/S083/evidence/raw/source/readme.working.snapshot:258: trailing whitespace.
+| S041 | **Short HTTP request at cutover:** Complete a request already admitted by the old deployment. |
learning/S083/evidence/raw/source/readme.working.snapshot:259: trailing whitespace.
+| S042 | **Long-running HTTP request:** Drain within supported limits or use durable asynchronous work without losing the user's operation. |
learning/S083/evidence/raw/source/readme.working.snapshot:260: trailing whitespace.
+| S043 | **Multipart upload:** Preserve uploaded parts and resume safely if ownership changes. |
learning/S083/evidence/raw/source/readme.working.snapshot:261: trailing whitespace.
+| S044 | **Large download:** Preserve completion or correct range-based resumption within the accepted user-experience budget. |
learning/S083/evidence/raw/source/readme.working.snapshot:262: trailing whitespace.
+| S045 | **WebSocket migration:** Preserve state and message sequencing; reconnection is seamless only if it meets agreed UX criteria. |
learning/S083/evidence/raw/source/readme.working.snapshot:263: trailing whitespace.
+| S046 | **Server-sent events:** Resume from an event cursor without missing or duplicating user-visible events. |
learning/S083/evidence/raw/source/readme.working.snapshot:264: trailing whitespace.
+| S047 | **gRPC streaming:** Provide application-level continuation where infrastructure cannot preserve the original stream. |
learning/S083/evidence/raw/source/readme.working.snapshot:265: trailing whitespace.
+| S048 | **Batch job retirement:** Finish or checkpoint work before retiring its host. |
learning/S083/evidence/raw/source/readme.working.snapshot:266: trailing whitespace.
+| S049 | **Ambiguous POST completion:** Prevent duplicate business effects when a committed request loses its response and is retried. |
learning/S083/evidence/raw/source/readme.working.snapshot:267: trailing whitespace.
+| S050 | **Stale keep-alive or pinned client:** Keep the old destination usable until its remaining traffic has been accounted for. |
learning/S083/evidence/raw/source/readme.working.snapshot:268: trailing whitespace.
+
learning/S083/evidence/raw/source/readme.working.snapshot:269: trailing whitespace.
+### F. N-tier and version compatibility
learning/S083/evidence/raw/source/readme.working.snapshot:270: trailing whitespace.
+
learning/S083/evidence/raw/source/readme.working.snapshot:271: trailing whitespace.
+| ID | Scenario and required behavior |
learning/S083/evidence/raw/source/readme.working.snapshot:272: trailing whitespace.
+| --- | --- |
learning/S083/evidence/raw/source/readme.working.snapshot:273: trailing whitespace.
+| S051 | **Old frontend to new API:** Preserve contracts used by already-open browser pages. |
learning/S083/evidence/raw/source/readme.working.snapshot:274: trailing whitespace.
+| S052 | **New frontend to old API:** Remain compatible while routing propagation leaves requests on the old backend. |
learning/S083/evidence/raw/source/readme.working.snapshot:275: trailing whitespace.
+| S053 | **Breaking API introduction:** Use versioned endpoints or transitional adapters instead of abruptly changing a live contract. |
learning/S083/evidence/raw/source/readme.working.snapshot:276: trailing whitespace.
+| S054 | **Database expand-migrate-contract:** Add compatible structures, migrate safely, and remove old structures only after old consumers disappear. |
learning/S083/evidence/raw/source/readme.working.snapshot:277: trailing whitespace.
+| S055 | **Cache payload evolution:** Version or translate cached objects so mixed application versions can coexist. |
learning/S083/evidence/raw/source/readme.working.snapshot:278: trailing whitespace.
+| S056 | **Event-schema evolution:** Ensure new producers remain compatible with old consumers during overlap. |
learning/S083/evidence/raw/source/readme.working.snapshot:279: trailing whitespace.
+| S057 | **Static-asset versioning:** Keep assets referenced by old HTML available after deployment. |
learning/S083/evidence/raw/source/readme.working.snapshot:280: trailing whitespace.
+| S058 | **Workflow/orchestration evolution:** Pin or explicitly version long-lived workflows so new code does not invalidate existing execution history. |
learning/S083/evidence/raw/source/readme.working.snapshot:281: trailing whitespace.
+| S059 | **Configuration-version overlap:** Ensure old and new code interpret shared flags and configuration consistently. |
learning/S083/evidence/raw/source/readme.working.snapshot:282: trailing whitespace.
+| S060 | **Rollback after schema evolution:** Preserve old-version compatibility or use explicit forward recovery when reversal is unsafe. |
learning/S083/evidence/raw/source/readme.working.snapshot:283: trailing whitespace.
+
learning/S083/evidence/raw/source/readme.working.snapshot:284: trailing whitespace.
+### G. Database and persistent-data scaling
learning/S083/evidence/raw/source/readme.working.snapshot:285: trailing whitespace.
+
learning/S083/evidence/raw/source/readme.working.snapshot:286: trailing whitespace.
+| ID | Scenario and required behavior |
learning/S083/evidence/raw/source/readme.working.snapshot:287: trailing whitespace.
+| --- | --- |
learning/S083/evidence/raw/source/readme.working.snapshot:288: trailing whitespace.
+| S061 | **Read-replica expansion:** Offload eligible reads while preserving required read-your-writes and freshness guarantees. |
learning/S083/evidence/raw/source/readme.working.snapshot:289: trailing whitespace.
+| S062 | **Connection-pool multiplication:** Keep aggregate database connections within limits as frontend/API instance counts increase. |
learning/S083/evidence/raw/source/readme.working.snapshot:290: trailing whitespace.
+| S063 | **Database vertical scaling:** Validate reconnects and transaction recovery; use parallel capacity if the operation exceeds interruption budgets. |
learning/S083/evidence/raw/source/readme.working.snapshot:291: trailing whitespace.
+| S064 | **New shard introduction:** Copy and synchronize data before changing routing, with unambiguous write ownership. |
learning/S083/evidence/raw/source/readme.working.snapshot:292: trailing whitespace.
+| S065 | **Hot-shard rebalancing:** Move tenants or partitions without missing writes or assigning two active owners. |
learning/S083/evidence/raw/source/readme.working.snapshot:293: trailing whitespace.
+| S066 | **Database failover during commit:** Reconcile uncertain outcomes without applying a transaction twice. |
learning/S083/evidence/raw/source/readme.working.snapshot:294: trailing whitespace.
+| S067 | **Replica lag during migration:** Route consistency-sensitive reads appropriately rather than silently returning unacceptable stale data. |
learning/S083/evidence/raw/source/readme.working.snapshot:295: trailing whitespace.
+| S068 | **Index creation under load:** Use supported online operations or reject changes whose locking behavior violates user budgets. |
learning/S083/evidence/raw/source/readme.working.snapshot:296: trailing whitespace.
+| S069 | **Writer handoff:** Fence the previous writer before accepting writes through the replacement. |
learning/S083/evidence/raw/source/readme.working.snapshot:297: trailing whitespace.
+| S070 | **Replica restoration and promotion:** Verify synchronization through required committed data before promoting restored capacity. |
learning/S083/evidence/raw/source/readme.working.snapshot:298: trailing whitespace.
+
learning/S083/evidence/raw/source/readme.working.snapshot:299: trailing whitespace.
+### H. Caches, queues, and background workers
learning/S083/evidence/raw/source/readme.working.snapshot:300: trailing whitespace.
+
learning/S083/evidence/raw/source/readme.working.snapshot:301: trailing whitespace.
+| ID | Scenario and required behavior |
learning/S083/evidence/raw/source/readme.working.snapshot:302: trailing whitespace.
+| --- | --- |
learning/S083/evidence/raw/source/readme.working.snapshot:303: trailing whitespace.
+| S071 | **Shared-cache expansion:** Scale cache capacity while keeping application access and payload compatibility intact. |
learning/S083/evidence/raw/source/readme.working.snapshot:304: trailing whitespace.
+| S072 | **Cache stampede after cutover:** Coalesce or limit refill work so cold caches do not overload the database. |
learning/S083/evidence/raw/source/readme.working.snapshot:305: trailing whitespace.
+| S073 | **Cache unavailable:** Use a tested durable recovery path that meets budgets; never silently substitute empty user state. |
learning/S083/evidence/raw/source/readme.working.snapshot:306: trailing whitespace.
+| S074 | **Session/cache eviction pressure:** Prevent capacity changes from unexpectedly losing required user state. |
learning/S083/evidence/raw/source/readme.working.snapshot:307: trailing whitespace.
+| S075 | **Consumer scale-out:** Coordinate partitions, locks, and deduplication as additional workers begin consuming. |
learning/S083/evidence/raw/source/readme.working.snapshot:308: trailing whitespace.
+| S076 | **Consumer scale-in:** Finish, renew, or safely relinquish claimed work before shutdown. |
learning/S083/evidence/raw/source/readme.working.snapshot:309: trailing whitespace.
+| S077 | **Message redelivery:** Preserve one business effect even when the broker delivers a message again. |
learning/S083/evidence/raw/source/readme.working.snapshot:310: trailing whitespace.
+| S078 | **Duplicate schedulers across deployments:** Use suitable ownership leases and fencing to prevent duplicate scheduled work. |
learning/S083/evidence/raw/source/readme.working.snapshot:311: trailing whitespace.
+| S079 | **Backlog surge:** Add processing capacity while maintaining ordering and completion-deadline requirements. |
learning/S083/evidence/raw/source/readme.working.snapshot:312: trailing whitespace.
+| S080 | **Partition reassignment:** Transfer checkpoints and ownership without missing events. |
learning/S083/evidence/raw/source/readme.working.snapshot:313: trailing whitespace.
+
learning/S083/evidence/raw/source/readme.working.snapshot:314: trailing whitespace.
+### I. State machine and orchestration correctness
learning/S083/evidence/raw/source/readme.working.snapshot:315: trailing whitespace.
+
learning/S083/evidence/raw/source/readme.working.snapshot:316: trailing whitespace.
+| ID | Scenario and required behavior |
learning/S083/evidence/raw/source/readme.working.snapshot:317: trailing whitespace.
+| --- | --- |
learning/S083/evidence/raw/source/readme.working.snapshot:318: trailing whitespace.
+| S081 | **Durable lifecycle tracking:** Record deployment identity, readiness, routing participation, draining, and retirement explicitly. |
learning/S083/evidence/raw/source/readme.working.snapshot:319: trailing whitespace.
+| S082 | **Stale controller update:** Reject an old deployment epoch attempting to change current routing or readiness. |
learning/S083/evidence/raw/source/readme.working.snapshot:320: trailing whitespace.
+| S083 | **Controller restart:** Resume from durable state without repeating a destructive transition. |
learning/S083/evidence/raw/source/readme.working.snapshot:321: trailing whitespace.
+| S084 | **Duplicate command delivery:** Make provisioning, routing, and cleanup retries idempotent; do not accidentally perform two swaps. |
learning/S083/evidence/raw/source/readme.working.snapshot:322: trailing whitespace.
+| S085 | **Concurrent deployment pipelines:** Serialize or conditionally coordinate changes to the same production destination. |
learning/S083/evidence/raw/source/readme.working.snapshot:323: trailing whitespace.
+| S086 | **Expired readiness evidence:** Revalidate health before promotion when readiness information becomes stale. |
learning/S083/evidence/raw/source/readme.working.snapshot:324: trailing whitespace.
+| S087 | **Partially applied routing change:** Verify effective routing and retain required old capacity until convergence is established. |
learning/S083/evidence/raw/source/readme.working.snapshot:325: trailing whitespace.
+| S088 | **Permission failure:** Surface the failure and preserve existing traffic rather than reporting success. |
learning/S083/evidence/raw/source/readme.working.snapshot:326: trailing whitespace.
+| S089 | **Control-plane outage:** Keep established data-plane routes serving without requiring the controller for every request. |
learning/S083/evidence/raw/source/readme.working.snapshot:327: trailing whitespace.
+| S090 | **Out-of-order cleanup:** Reject retirement while traffic, work, state ownership, or rollback requirements depend on the deployment. |
learning/S083/evidence/raw/source/readme.working.snapshot:328: trailing whitespace.
+
learning/S083/evidence/raw/source/readme.working.snapshot:329: trailing whitespace.
+### J. Failure containment and rollback
learning/S083/evidence/raw/source/readme.working.snapshot:330: trailing whitespace.
+
learning/S083/evidence/raw/source/readme.working.snapshot:331: trailing whitespace.
+| ID | Scenario and required behavior |
learning/S083/evidence/raw/source/readme.working.snapshot:332: trailing whitespace.
+| --- | --- |
learning/S083/evidence/raw/source/readme.working.snapshot:333: trailing whitespace.
+| S091 | **Candidate crashes during warm-up:** Abort before exposure while production continues serving. |
learning/S083/evidence/raw/source/readme.working.snapshot:334: trailing whitespace.
+| S092 | **Candidate fails during canary:** Stop further exposure and reverse routing; count interruptions already experienced. |
learning/S083/evidence/raw/source/readme.working.snapshot:335: trailing whitespace.
+| S093 | **Latency regression without errors:** Reject a candidate that returns successful responses too slowly. |
learning/S083/evidence/raw/source/readme.working.snapshot:336: trailing whitespace.
+| S094 | **Authentication regression:** Detect login/session failures before expanding the affected cohort. |
learning/S083/evidence/raw/source/readme.working.snapshot:337: trailing whitespace.
+| S095 | **Candidate dependency partition:** Remove it from new admission and retain a usable compatible destination. |
learning/S083/evidence/raw/source/readme.working.snapshot:338: trailing whitespace.
+| S096 | **Shared-plan resource contention:** Demonstrate sufficient overlap headroom or isolate deployments into separate plans. |
learning/S083/evidence/raw/source/readme.working.snapshot:339: trailing whitespace.
+| S097 | **Rollback destination becomes cold:** Keep rollback capacity ready throughout its promised retention window. |
learning/S083/evidence/raw/source/readme.working.snapshot:340: trailing whitespace.
+| S098 | **Rollback after new writes:** Preserve and interpret data created by the new version. |
learning/S083/evidence/raw/source/readme.working.snapshot:341: trailing whitespace.
+| S099 | **Rollback command fails:** Inspect effective state and preserve known-good routing rather than blindly reversing again. |
learning/S083/evidence/raw/source/readme.working.snapshot:342: trailing whitespace.
+| S100 | **Forced termination:** Verify that lost work is detected and counted, not misclassified as a successful transition. |
learning/S083/evidence/raw/source/readme.working.snapshot:343: trailing whitespace.
+
learning/S083/evidence/raw/source/readme.working.snapshot:344: trailing whitespace.
+### K. Networking, configuration, and edge routing
learning/S083/evidence/raw/source/readme.working.snapshot:345: trailing whitespace.
+
learning/S083/evidence/raw/source/readme.working.snapshot:346: trailing whitespace.
+| ID | Scenario and required behavior |
learning/S083/evidence/raw/source/readme.working.snapshot:347: trailing whitespace.
+| --- | --- |
learning/S083/evidence/raw/source/readme.working.snapshot:348: trailing whitespace.
+| S101 | **Stable public endpoint:** Keep the user-facing hostname constant while changing backend destinations. |
learning/S083/evidence/raw/source/readme.working.snapshot:349: trailing whitespace.
+| S102 | **DNS-cache persistence:** Keep cached destinations usable for the required overlap period; do not assume immediate DNS convergence. |
learning/S083/evidence/raw/source/readme.working.snapshot:350: trailing whitespace.
+| S103 | **TLS/certificate continuity:** Ensure every eligible destination supports the required hostname and trust configuration. |
learning/S083/evidence/raw/source/readme.working.snapshot:351: trailing whitespace.
+| S104 | **Host-header and redirect differences:** Prevent warm-up success from hiding production redirect or callback failures. |
learning/S083/evidence/raw/source/readme.working.snapshot:352: trailing whitespace.
+| S105 | **Non-swapped configuration:** Validate managed identity, networking, and other slot-specific properties at the effective destination. |
learning/S083/evidence/raw/source/readme.working.snapshot:353: trailing whitespace.
+| S106 | **Private endpoint/private DNS:** Test the real application access path, not only an externally reachable probe. |
learning/S083/evidence/raw/source/readme.working.snapshot:354: trailing whitespace.
+| S107 | **CORS differences:** Preserve browser access for existing origins throughout migration. |
learning/S083/evidence/raw/source/readme.working.snapshot:355: trailing whitespace.
+| S108 | **WAF/policy differences:** Ensure valid candidate application requests and assets are not unexpectedly blocked. |
learning/S083/evidence/raw/source/readme.working.snapshot:356: trailing whitespace.
+| S109 | **Outbound connection/SNAT pressure:** Maintain sufficient outbound connectivity as instance and connection counts grow. |
learning/S083/evidence/raw/source/readme.working.snapshot:357: trailing whitespace.
+| S110 | **Edge configuration propagation:** Retain old origins until routing changes have converged sufficiently for safe retirement. |
learning/S083/evidence/raw/source/readme.working.snapshot:358: trailing whitespace.
